// Patch 270, Stage 2: MOVED UP, from just after sv_saveloc.qc.
//
// QuakeC has no forward declarations, so a file can only read globals that an
// earlier file declared.  Stage 2 makes the timer, the recorder and the
// save-loc list behave differently in a lobby, which means sv_timer.qc and
// sv_saveloc.qc have to be able to read lobby_on -- and it was declared after
// them.  The alternative was a second copy of the cvar reads in each file,
// which is the shape that produced the ui_rs_armed bug this tree already ate.
//
// Safe to move because sv_lobby.qc depends on NOTHING in this project: grep it
// and every identifier it touches is either its own lobby_ prefix or an engine
// builtin/field from defs/sv_defs.qc.  It is only ever CALLED from later files
// (sv_player.qc's connect/disconnect, sv_main.qc's frame), and calls still run
// downhill.
server/sv_lobby.qc
// Event fog owns per-player mode; the timer below latches its whole-run fact.
server/sv_eventfog.qc
// Patch 372: the map clock's votes.  After sv_lobby.qc, whose Lobby_Cycle state
// it writes; sv_player.qc and sv_main.qc below call into it.
server/sv_vote.qc

server/sv_archive_decl.qc
server/sv_timer.qc
server/sv_saveloc.qc
// Movement-policy builders; sv_warpop.qc publishes the reset answers (Patch 753).
server/sv_moveprep.qc
// Patch 753: after moveprep (SV_MovePrepReset); sv_player.qc calls it
server/sv_warpop.qc
server/sv_resume.qc
// Patch 383: the pose stream.  After sv_timer.qc (run_movetick, SV_RecKeys),
// sv_saveloc.qc (rec_sl_hold) and sv_lobby.qc; sv_player.qc and sv_main.qc call it.
server/sv_pose.qc
// Patch 615: Steam accounts.  After sv_lobby.qc (Lobby_Active; its
// URI_Get_Callback holds the prototype) and sv_timer.qc (SV_RecIsHex); before
// sv_player.qc, which calls it from the command dispatch and ClientConnect.
server/sv_social.qc
server/sv_account.qc
server/sv_viewmodel.qc
server/sv_inventory.qc
server/sv_publictime.qc
